  m_text: 'Mexico is home to a unique plant known as Impatiens mexicana. While many
    people are familiar with garden Busy Lizzies, this specific species is special
    because it grows naturally in the cool, misty mountain forests of Mexico.


    This
    plant plays an important role in nature. Its bright flowers provide food for
    local birds and insects, which helps keep the entire forest ecosystem healthy.
    For scientists, it is a perfect example of how plants adapt over time to survive
    in very specific environments. It reminds us why protecting natural habitats
    is so important for the world''s biodiversity.'
